{
  "id": "interior-farmhouse-v1",
  "description": "Tier A interior kit for vanilla farmhouse cells (decision 0103 decision 3): the interior tileset pieces, furniture, containers, clutter, carried items and light-bearing meshes that the tier A cells claimed on published places reference, and that no other published kit already holds. The set is read from the cells themselves by `worldgen.export_interior_bundle` (every `no-kit-asset` gap of a claimed cell), never picked by name. First cell: Skyrim.esm DawnstarBrinasHouse, the claim on Claywater Station's station house (farmhouse01). A later claim adds its gaps here and rebuilds. The full farmhouse interior tileset (`vanilla-farmhouse-int`, 76 pieces including the basement family) stays an unbuilt config for Phase 12's assembled interiors. Walk 3 lane L14 (2026-09-28): the gaps of every vanilla-shell and King of the Murkmire cell linked to a culture-pool shell whose only acceptance failure was a missing clutter, furniture or item mesh were added (the vault's vanilla archives), so those cells export whole.",
  "culture": "imperial-colonial",
  "output": "tooling/asset-pipeline/output/kits/interior-farmhouse-v1.glb",
  "lodRatios": [
    0.35,
    0.12
  ],
  "textureMaxSize": 512,
  "publish": true,
  "compression": {
    "color": "etc1s"
  },
  "compressionReason": "Interior clutter kit (planner ruling 9, interiors round 2): colour textures ETC1S, normal and attribute maps stay UASTC. Interior kits are mostly small clutter seen at arm's length under point lights, where ETC1S's block error (22-33 dB, docs/research/rendering/gpu-texture-and-mesh-compression.md) was judged acceptable against the per-cell download; foliage cards and exterior kits keep UASTC.",
